From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: don't clear clock_stop_not_supported on enumeration

The flag was cleared for every enumerated device, so a bogus device ID
read after the amps turned clock stop back on. The WSA881x amps then miss
the clock stop exit and fail to attach. Only ever set it.

---
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -665,7 +665,6 @@
 
 		sdw_extract_slave_id(bus, addr, &id);
 		found = false;
-		ctrl->clock_stop_not_supported = false;
 		/* Now compare with entries */
 		list_for_each_entry_safe(slave, _s, &bus->slaves, node) {
 			if (sdw_compare_devid(slave, id) == 0) {
